<title>JAPAN: Nisshin Oil says to build new plant.</title>
<headline>Nisshin Oil says to build new plant.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's largest edible oil producer Nisshin Oil Mills Ltd on Thursday confirmed a newspaper report that it has decided to build a plant in Sakai, western Japan.</p>
<p>At the initial stage of the project, Nisshin will invest about 3.5 billion yen to build the plant for production and distribution. The plant is scheduled to start operating in January 1998.</p>
<p>The new plant will be capable of refining 200 tonnes a day, the company said in a statement.</p>
